# MedTracker Development Tasks

## Phase 1: Planning and Setup
- [ ] Write implementation plan for DB and Auth flow.
- [ ] Review implementation plan with User.
- [ ] Set up MySQL database and `users` table schema.

## Phase 2: Backend Development (PHP)
- [ ] Create `config.php` for database connection.
- [ ] Create `signup.php` to handle user registration (Admin, Health Worker, User).
- [ ] Create `login.php` to handle authentication via Phone and Password.
- [ ] Set up PHPMailer for OTP emails.
- [ ] Create `forgot_password.php` to generate and send OTP.
- [ ] Create `reset_password.php` to verify OTP and update password.

## Phase 3: Frontend Development (HTML/JS/CSS)
- [ ] Create `index.html` (Get Started page) with premium medicine reminder aesthetics.
- [ ] Create `role_selection.html` (Choose role for Login/Signup).
- [ ] Create `signup.html` (Dynamic form fields based on role: Name, Phone, Email, Password, Post/Relation).
- [ ] Create `login.html` (Phone and Password).
- [ ] Create `forgot_password.html` and `reset_password.html` for OTP flow.
- [ ] Create `dashboard.html` (Placeholder after login).
- [ ] Write `css/style.css` for a beautiful, modern, dynamic design.
- [ ] Write `js/script.js` for form validation, dynamic toggling of inputs, and AJAX requests.

## Phase 4: Verification
- [ ] Test Database creation.
- [ ] Test Signup for each role.
- [ ] Test Login flow.
- [ ] Test Forgot Password (OTP) flow.
